This repository and all works derived from it are dual-licensed under:

1. Fountain of Love License v2.0, which states the ethical, anti-capture, stewardship, and value-flow conditions.
2. Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), where applicable, as an additional public licensing layer.

Where both licenses apply, the stricter condition or the condition providing greater protection against privatization, extraction, or institutional capture governs the use.

This license is not a substitute for legal advice. It states the intent and permission conditions under which the work is offered.

## 1. Purpose

The Fountain of Love License (FoL) ensures that this work and all derivative works serve individuals, communities, and the planet. It prevents private, corporate, academic, governmental, or institutional capture, including capture through money, authority, ownership, prestige, exclusivity, or decision-making power.

The purpose of this license is to keep knowledge, methods, software, designs, and innovations in the commons, available for shared learning and regenerative use.

## 2. Permissions

You may:

* Use, study, copy, and build upon this work for personal, educational, research, or community benefit.
* Use this work in non-profit projects, provided that attribution, transparency, redistribution, and value-flows are provided.
* Use this work in academic contexts for open teaching, open research, peer learning, public scholarship, and non-extractive collaboration.
* Use this work in for-profit, revenue-generating, or institutionally beneficial contexts only under a formal Franchise, Stewardship, or Contributor Agreement in preference with the Fountain of Love steward organization.

All permissions are conditional on compliance with this license.

## 3. Definitions

### 3.1 Covered Work

"Covered Work" means this repository, its text, code, diagrams, methods, concepts, designs, models, documentation, and any derivative, adaptation, extension, implementation, training material, curriculum, publication, service, product, or institutional process that substantially relies on them.

### 3.2 Economic Benefit

"Economic Benefit" means any financial or resource advantage obtained through use of the Covered Work, whether direct or indirect.

Economic Benefit includes, without limitation:

* revenue, profit, licensing fees, consulting fees, service fees, tuition, subscriptions, grants, sponsorships, donations, or investment value;
* cost reductions, avoided labor, avoided licensing fees, operational savings, efficiency gains, budget substitution, or institutional cost cutting;
* academic monetization, including paid courses, credential programs, funded research, proprietary training, grant-funded deliverables, institutionally owned outputs, restricted datasets, or exclusive research infrastructure;
* reputational, career, ranking, citation, admissions, enrollment, procurement, or fundraising advantage when used as a basis for institutional accumulation or exclusionary control.

Economic Benefit is not limited to private companies. It also applies to universities, research institutes, foundations, laboratories, schools, public bodies, non-profits, and other institutions.

### 3.3 Surplus

"Surplus" means Economic Benefit remaining after reasonable, documented, good-faith costs and sufficiency-based compensation have been accounted for.

Sufficiency-based compensation means compensation that is comfortable and dignified, but not extractive or accumulative. The suggested maximum individual compensation threshold is EUR 14,000 per month, or a local equivalent adjusted for cost of living and role responsibility.

Surplus beyond that threshold must flow back to the steward pool described in Section 6.

### 3.4 Steward Organization

"Steward Organization" means a non-profit steward entity, or its formally recognized successor or aligned network node, operating under the Fountain of Love Operating Model:

https://github.com/fountain-of-love/operating-model

Preferences goes out to founding a Fountain of Love non-profit entity.
## 4. Absolute Restrictions

You may not:

* use, sell, license, host, package, teach, publish, or incorporate the Covered Work for private or institutional Economic Benefit without a formal stewardship;
* use the Covered Work to reduce costs, replace labor, attract funding, create paid (academic) programs, support grant capture, or strengthen institutional budgets without honoring the surplus-return rules;
* claim, assert, register, or enforce patents, copyrights, trademarks, trade secrets, database rights, or other exclusive rights over the Covered Work or derivatives that substantially rely on it;
* use the Covered Work to accumulate authority, control, gatekeeping power, credentialing power, or decision-making power over others;
* modify, sublicense, or relicense the Covered Work under terms that enable commercialization, privatization, enclosure, or institutional capture;
* incorporate the Covered Work into closed, proprietary, surveillance-based, coercive, profit-extractive, or exclusionary systems.

Violation of these terms automatically terminates the violator's rights under this license.

## 5. Derivative Works

All derivative or extended works that build upon, reference, adapt, operationalize, teach, publish, or rely on the insight, theory, method, code, architecture, or materials of the Covered Work are subject to this license.

Derivative works must:

* remain open, non-commercial, and stewardship-aligned unless covered by a formal stewardship agreement;
* include this full license text;
* provide clear attribution to "Fountain of Love - Enigma Initiative";
* disclose any Economic Benefit, institutional advantage, funding stream, or cost reduction created through use of the Covered Work;
* avoid mechanisms that enable private capture, accumulation, hierarchy, credential monopoly, or institutional enclosure.

Combining the Covered Work with other works does not remove these obligations from the Covered Work or from derivatives substantially relying on it.

## 6. Redistribution and Value Flow

### 6.1 Principle of Flow

All Surplus created through use of the Covered Work must return to the commons through a non-profit steward pool or a formally aligned network node.

This includes Surplus created by commercial entities, non-profits, universities, research institutes, schools, laboratories, foundations, public bodies, and other institutions.

The steward pool should be governed according to the Fountain of Love Operating Model:

https://github.com/fountain-of-love/operating-model

### 6.2 Fair Compensation

Income derived from the Covered Work must be limited to sufficiency-based compensation: comfortable, dignified, transparent, and non-accumulative. Suggested maximum individual compensation: EUR 14,000 per month, or local equivalent. Surplus beyond that threshold must flow back to a non-profit steward pool.

### 6.3 Redistribution Ratios

Unless a written stewardship agreement with a non-profit steward pool based on the Fountain of Love Operating Model states otherwise:

* non-profit, educational, academic, and public-interest institutions may retain 13% of Surplus after reasonable documented costs and fair compensation;
* the remaining 87% of Surplus must be contributed to the Fountain of Love steward network for redistribution;
* for-profit entities may operate only through licensed stewardship franchises or equivalent written agreements under the same flow principles.

Cost savings and avoided expenses count as Economic Benefit when calculating Surplus.

## 7. Academic and Institutional Use

Academic, educational, and research use is welcome when it remains open, transparent, non-extractive, and commons-aligned. Academic and institutional users may not use the Covered Work to:

* create exclusive paid courses, proprietary curricula, certification monopolies, restricted research programs, or closed institutional assets;
* obtain grants, public funding, private funding, rankings, patents, career advancement, procurement advantage, or reputational gain while enclosing the resulting materials or benefits;
* reduce institutional costs, replace staff, centralize decision-making, or consolidate authority without treating the resulting savings or advantage as Economic Benefit;
* publish derivative scholarship while obscuring the work's origin, restricting access, or claiming exclusive intellectual ownership;
* use the Covered Work to strengthen centralized power, authority, budget control, or prestige within an academic or research institution.

Open academic publication, public teaching, and non-extractive research are permitted when attribution, openness, transparency, and surplus-return obligations are honored.

## 8. Patent and Authority Non-Assertion

1. Patent non-assertion: No party, including contributors, may claim or enforce patent rights over the Covered Work or derivatives substantially relying on it.
2. Defensive publication: The Covered Work is published as open prior art to help prevent exclusive claims over its concepts, architectures, methods, and theoretical frameworks.
3. Authority disarmament: No institution may use the Covered Work to build or justify governance models that impose power over others. Applications must remain cooperative, transparent, participatory, and accountable.
4. No exclusive rights: Any attempt to enclose the Covered Work through legal, academic, technical, or institutional mechanisms violates this license and terminates permission to use it.

## 9. Transparency and Oversight

Users, institutions, and stewards must operate in good faith and maintain transparent records concerning:

* use of the Covered Work;
* derivative works;
* funding, revenue, grants, donations, and sponsorships;
* cost savings, avoided expenses, and institutional gains;
* compensation and Surplus calculations;
* redistribution to the steward pool.

The Fountain of Love steward organization may request public disclosure of accounting and redistribution reports where needed to verify compliance. Entities that refuse reasonable transparency requests lose stewardship privileges and license rights.

## 10. Enforcement and Jurisdiction

Automatic termination applies to any breach of this license, including hidden monetization, undisclosed academic or institutional Economic Benefit, cost-saving extraction, authority accumulation, proprietary enclosure, or relicensing violations.

Upon violation, the violator must stop using the Covered Work and any derivative work that substantially relies on it until compliance is restored through written permission from the Steward Organization.

Legal venue: The Netherlands, European Union, under applicable law and the ethical governance principles of the Fountain of Love Operating Model.

Remedies may include injunction, mandatory attribution correction, mandatory public disclosure, accounting of Economic Benefit, redistribution of Surplus, and permanent disqualification from steward access.

## 11. Public Commons and Open Prior Art

This license is also a defensive publication. The concepts, architectures, methods, and theoretical frameworks in the Covered Work are made publicly available as open prior art. No entity may claim novelty, originality, exclusive ownership, or institutional control over them in any legal, academic, commercial, or administrative context.

This section does not waive the anti-capture, attribution, copyleft, stewardship, or redistribution obligations of this license.

## 12. Ethical Foundation

This license is legal in form and ethical in purpose. It embodies the role of the Steward: to protect flow, sufficiency, reciprocity, openness, and care.

The Fountain Principle:

> Value flows outward to nourish all.  
> Surplus returns inward to replenish the source.  
> Ownership gives way to shared stewardship.

Technology, knowledge, and institutions under this license must serve:

* regeneration over extraction;
* collaboration over domination;
* coherence over control;
* sufficiency over accumulation;
* stewardship over ownership.

## 13. Spirit of Interpretation

If a conflict arises between legal form and ethical intent, this license must be interpreted in the way that best preserves the commons, prevents capture, protects contributors, and returns Surplus to shared stewardship.

The preferred resolution path is dialogue, repair, transparency, and restoration of flow before adversarial enforcement.

